{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:45:47.404542Z","id":"d47d063427a74eb3f40efcbab5347d95fe067662d9b5322395d4292f6eb6c410","body":{"detail":"A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the cap. Checking the cap first (before the store) would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Test: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"fbad0c499e5bc28dc06376c136e461aa40241fa8ed0db246fca16dc0db578afd"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","tags":["revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:45:47.404574Z","id":"cd23aa71def277a1f270b669a41742ff986224aeb9650b8810d0519640ec23a9","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.3 gives each web error a retryable flag, but clax_bot_sandbox::HostError has only code and message, so from_web drops WebError::retryable. The model sees only the message.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":138},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"fbf7d76edf74006f9c735c98ebefd643d57ae1206018eaad22ccbf0dbc6cf7fd"},"suggested_fix":"Add retryable to HostError (and the sandbox's thrown error), or say 'try again' in the message of retryable errors.","summary":"A web error's retryable flag does not reach the script","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T05:45:47.404599Z","id":"aeca7a97397badcfdb1fb049659dd3126cf37f61c349b134112f7a48658c0eba","body":{"detail":"After a step is resumed, a replayed web call's CallLog gets web = {query} or {url} as the script passed it, with no source and cost_milli None, so the committed step payload (and the run panel built from it) loses where a replayed fetch's URL came from and what it cost. The bot.web audit record and the page store keep both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"42974242d12973ccc48e7b8159be101ce319f0c44a91e6d2fc6f0b8f9b2f4638"},"summary":"A web call answered from the journal shows its raw arguments and no source or cost","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T06:07:50.965784Z","id":"7f2e541540336c369c08b997a92510a6a6ad3f712f1f2b97bef7eab09176a929","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5dce9c70a","summary":"Fixed in git:5dce9c70a: a web call's journal entry keeps cost_milli, web ({url, source}) and, for a fetch, source and format beside the script's value, and from_entry answers a replay with them. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration passes web::a_resumed_fetch_answers_from_the_journal_with_its_source_and_cost (the resumed step's call shows {url, source: comment} and the charged row's credits).","supersedes":"aeca7a97397badcfdb1fb049659dd3126cf37f61c349b134112f7a48658c0eba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T06:07:51.217351Z","id":"b402f3964706873684cebfd95a650b929d69ea02a97390e23ac416e2eb56a1bb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cd23aa71def277a1f270b669a41742ff986224aeb9650b8810d0519640ec23a9","summary":"Interim since git:5dce9c70a: from_web (crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs) appends ' (retryable: try again)' to a retryable WebError's message, and a request context that cannot be read answers web_unavailable with the same words (test web::a_failed_search_is_free_and_a_failed_fetch_is_not). The script still gets no retryable field: HostError has none. Left open for that.","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T06:07:51.217786Z","id":"7091c9bd2aa393839a4348c21a8ec8cd7ecad9672ff5d9db392ea644dc3651b6","body":{"detail":"A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the fetch cap. Checking the cap first would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Tests: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store, a_stored_page_is_served_at_the_fetch_cap.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":559},"end":{"line":586},"content_hash":"a74708a321713ab92221074e982fb7d472b9c60b49e22d9d774ec927ff59c1b9"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","supersedes":"d47d063427a74eb3f40efcbab5347d95fe067662d9b5322395d4292f6eb6c410","tags":["revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T06:07:51.345332Z","id":"8ee1642785489d906addd6b4a5e149d9179a16a37f77b02fa4ee4ef12a988bc6","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §7.2: a search that fails is not charged, and the cap counts charged calls (RunHost::spent_counts reads the run's web.* usage rows). A script can call clax.web.search again and again while the provider answers errors; it is bounded only by the script's time and call limits and the run's step cap, at the instance's cost if the provider bills failures.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":525},"end":{"line":538},"content_hash":"fafefdce7a005479f0b6b15308a5437b81b4defc605cea9793369947ba427321"},"summary":"A failed search is neither charged nor counted, so a script may retry a provider that is down","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T06:07:51.345379Z","id":"158f36c436264967679a07f20d827b3c8cd8d92860a6d7bd4469ae3d3cdafdba","body":{"detail":"RunHost::url_source derives the sources (spec §5.2) at every fetch: one bot_calls read per step 1..=n plus web_pages, then the stored-page and format checks read from those. Fine at today's step caps (max_steps); a run with many steps or many large pages pays it per fetch. A run-wide bot_calls read, or a sources query in the store, would make it one read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":726},"end":{"line":737},"content_hash":"a1833251771d73f566b24b82c5fa247e01467282dc48785ef9ead676bb719b58"},"suggested_fix":"Add Store::bot_calls_of_run(run) and read the page store without page text for the source derivation.","summary":"Each fetch reads the whole run's journal, step by step, and its page store","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:30:16.108448Z","id":"54baa9f7366e080d92aeface5516016b8b6a6df22bdd5cbe4e1d3b43defa29c7","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.3 gives each web error a retryable flag, but clax_bot_sandbox::HostError has only code and message, so from_web drops WebError::retryable. The model sees only the message.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"9bfdac1630ee5fdf002cbbb44f4e4782dc76b048be561b4a3affba26b1fc029c"},"suggested_fix":"Add retryable to HostError (and the sandbox's thrown error), or say 'try again' in the message of retryable errors.","summary":"A web error's retryable flag does not reach the script","supersedes":"cd23aa71def277a1f270b669a41742ff986224aeb9650b8810d0519640ec23a9","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
